    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0015" n="9" xml:id="pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">641.5531/22: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-03">June 3,
                        1942</date>.<lb/>[Received June 3—1:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3092. Department’s 1094 March 16. Embassy’s 1362 and 1396 of March 21 and 24
                    respectively.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>Foreign Office has today informed Embassy that renewal of Anglo-Belgian
                        agreement to September 1, 1942, with respect to finance and purchase of
                        commodities from Belgian Congo, will be signed tomorrow.<anchor n="11"
                            xml:id="d10-f1"/>
                    </item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>Embassy’s 2798, May 20. As no reply has been received to this telegram
                        Foreign Office is omitting reference to United States Government in section
                        2. Otherwise this letter will be handed to Belgian authorities tomorrow
                        unaltered.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d10-f1" n="11" xml:id="d10-f1-content">
                <p>Signed June 4, 1942; for text, see British Cmd. 6365, Treaty Series No. 1 (1942):
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Agreement … renewing the arrangements for the
                        Regulation of Purchases of Commodities from the Belgian Congo and Ruanda
                        Urundi</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
